  "title": "Hurricane Maria Relief 5",
  "description": "B-roll of unloading pallets and rescue equipment off a C-5M. At the request of civil authorities, an aircrew from the 22nd Airlift Squadron loaded and flew a C-5M Super Galaxy from March Air Reserve Base, Calif., to San Juan, Puerto Rico. The Super Galaxy transported members of Task Force 2, Task Force 6, and Task Force 7 from the California Search and Rescue Team as well as their equipment to provide aid to Puerto Rico in the aftermath of Hurricane Maria.",
